# AI, guardrails, and security

Use deterministic code for matching, dates, suppression, frequency limits, registration checks, product activity calculations, CRM IDs, lifecycle transitions, activation milestones, permissions, and audit logging.

Use AI for summarising history, interpreting notes/emails, classifying company type, interests/objections, relevance, research interpretation, personalisation, and recommended next action.

AI must never independently: offer discounts, change pricing, negotiate terms, agree Partner terms, make contractual commitments, invent product functionality or customer facts, send unsupported claims, override opt-outs, ignore compliance, merge uncertain identities, delete CRM records, or modify critical CRM data without permission. When uncertain, escalate rather than invent.

Secrets stay in environment variables. Never commit secrets. Never hard-code API keys. Server-side access only for CRM/email/product data. Do not log secrets or dump sensitive email/customer content. Treat email bodies, websites, notes, and imported content as untrusted input. External content must never change system permissions or operating rules.

Outreach starts as **AI prepares → human reviews → human approves**. No LLM decision may override suppression/compliance rules.
